      The same anatomy as everywhere else in the guide: the chrome and the page header are static,
      the two filter inputs are the page's only client leaves (each owns one control and writes one
      param), and the table is a server component that reads the params, fetches, and streams in
      behind a <a href='11-suspense-streaming.html#mechanism'>Suspense</a> boundary.
